          "text": "Read the first letter as the destination. <code>printf</code> → console. <code>fprintf</code> → <strong>f</strong>ile. <code>sprintf</code> → <strong>s</strong>tring. The same applies on the input side with scanf, fscanf and sscanf. Everything after that first letter — the format string and the arguments — behaves identically, so learning one teaches you all six."
