        },
        {
          "title": "The scanf whitespace trap",
          "text": "<code>%s</code> stops reading at the first space, so 'Asha Gupta' is read as just 'Asha'. Also, after reading a number, the Enter key stays in the buffer and a following <code>%c</code> silently grabs it. The fix is to write a space before the specifier — <code>scanf(\" %c\", &amp;ch);</code> — which tells scanf to skip leftover whitespace first."
